{
 "comment": "party_monthly's money reason (owner ruling 7b, as the reference applies it at da9e2d3d), every voucher in the books and the Trial Balance tying in every block. Indirect expenses: a supplier paid in cash with rent credited on the cash's side (a credit line read by its side); a receipt net of bank charges from two customers (several parties); a receipt net of charges that also pays a supplier, so the bank nets to the other side but one bank line is on the charges' side (gross, not net); a round-off on a receipt (a stated limit); a round-off on a cash sales invoice, the customer's though cash is on its side (invoice-class); rent with the bank on the supplier's side, the supplier's; rent reversed to a supplier beside a nil bank line, the supplier's (a nil line is on neither side). Sales and purchases: a journal sale beside a cash line on the sales' side, and a payment with purchases credited beside the bank, each the party's (the money reason is for the expense blocks only). Direct expenses: three receipts net of collection charges, two identical (one GUID, number, date and lines) and one with no GUID, each counted and cited, and a supplier paid with freight on its side and no GUID (not on the other side, with the expense example).",
